KG42.register("source_edge_archive-42e9ae90673e5ed8c978bb09",{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E002","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","rule_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E002","source":"pricing.local","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"precedes","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g03-E01"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C004"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-84de1f1af39d310b","target":"COMP-276b46f772c03e0a","source_occurrence_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","target_occurrence_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal","source_unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","target_unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Buyer consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Preparation of internal price signals for the next time slot in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Price-mediated consumption decisions of PV prosumers in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Seller consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g03-E01"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"27187fdc2890ef1b54fca5749d6eefc48a610f0b488b5425a5ec990519124b8b","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"The MGO determines the internal buying and selling prices simultaneously and obtains next-slot prices by solving the pricing optimization. Scope: Stackelberg ESM internal buying and selling prices for the next time slot. The MGO increases the internal selling price p_s in the reported shortage cases. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16. Condition: Selling energy is less than buying energy in these reported time slots. The MGO decreases the internal buying price p_b in the reported surplus cases. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 13 and 14. Condition: Selling energy is more than buying energy in these reported time slots. Internal buying and selling prices are decision variables for maximizing the MGO's own profit, subject to λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. Scope: Stackelberg ESM internal-price optimization. Initial internal selling and buying prices may be set to λ^s and λ^b, respectively. Scope: Initialization of internal prices for each time slot. Condition: Initial price setting. Select the internal price pair by comparing MGO profit at the optima of D_1 and D_2, where D_1 applies when E^b \u003c E^s and D_2 applies when E^b ≥ E^s. Scope: Selection of optimal internal prices across the surplus and nonsurplus pricing regions. The internal selling and buying prices remain at λ^s and λ^b, respectively, in these reported time slots. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 7 and 17–19 only. Condition: PV energy is entirely self-consumed and no energy is feasible to trade inside the microgrid.","target_definition":"Internal buying and selling prices coordinate decentralized consumption decisions: prosumers adjust their consumption and choose optimal consumption in response to these prices. Scope: Price-mediated consumption decisions of PV prosumers in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. An increase in p_s may induce sellers to reduce consumption and thereby increase the energy they sell. Scope: Seller consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. Condition: The internal selling price p_s increases. A decrease in p_b may induce buyers to increase consumption and thereby increase the energy they buy. Scope: Buyer consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. Condition: The internal buying price p_b decreases. The MGO solves the internal-price optimization before distributing the resulting internal prices to all prosumers as coordination signals. Scope: Preparation of internal price signals for the next time slot in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The MGO solves the internal-price optimization before distributing the resulting internal prices to all prosumers as coordination signals. Scope: Preparation of internal price signals for the next time slot in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g03-E01"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e019","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.C Implementation Process","anchor_text":"n- set as λs and λb, respectively. 2) Every prosumer submits ˆEgn, kn, and the role of buyer or re s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Considering (26) and (27) belong to nonlinear programming problem, the MGO can solve (30) and obtain the internal prices p_s and p_b for the next time slot by using interior point method. The MGO broadcasts the internal prices of next time slot to all the prosumers;"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p09-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"V.F Analysis of Practical Implementation and Feasibility","anchor_text":"and thus lower the impact on the utility grid. du co F. Analysis of Practical Implementation and Fea","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"As the method is implemented by centralized optimization, the prosumers are only required to submit E_n^g, k_n, and role attribute. Meanwhile, the MGO needs to solve problem (30), and then distributes the internal prices p_s and p_b to all the prosumers. Thus, the bidirectional data exchange between MGO and prosumers are only several bytes of data, which can be easily achieved with the monitoring and control system of microgrids."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Buyer consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Preparation of internal price signals for the next time slot in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Price-mediated consumption decisions of PV prosumers in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM. | Seller consumption responses to internal prices in the Stackelberg microgrid ESM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g03-E01"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E002","source":"pricing.local","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"precedes","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g03-E01"]},"paper_scope_note":"Stackelberg ESM, deviation billing, and the Cournot baseline are kept separate; buying/selling branches, numerical cases, and the no-deviation/penalty conditions are retained with the declaration."}});
